#[doc("""
The document as a value: the intermediate form between source text and
ANSI lines. Pure and effect-free — derived `Eq` and `Show` are what let
the parser be tested by structural equality.
""")]

#[doc("""
Content within a line. `Text` is the literal, already stripped of its
markup. The block phase produces only `Text`; the inline scanner
replaces those nodes with the tree of emphasis, code and links.
""")]
#[derive(Eq, Show)]
pub type Inline =
    Text(String)
  | Emph([Inline])
  | Strong([Inline])
  | CodeSpan(String)
  | Link([Inline], String)

#[doc("""
A top-level block. `Code` carries the fence language (empty when none
was declared) and its raw lines, never reinterpreted. `Bullets` and
`Ordered` hold each item as a list of blocks, which is what allows
paragraphs and sublists to nest inside an item. `Ordered` remembers the
number the list started at.
""")]
#[derive(Eq, Show)]
pub type Block =
    Heading(Int, [Inline])
  | Para([Inline])
  | Code(String, [String])
  | Quote([Block])
  | Bullets([[Block]])
  | Ordered(Int, [[Block]])
  | Rule
